step_details.raw_response:
Thought: Test a simple mean of all 19 models to see if a robust average beats the best single.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"mean","pool":"pool_full"}

Thought: Test a weighted combination using inverse error on the full pool to see if weighting improves over simple mean.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: Test a weighted combination using the pooled_meta_model handle (w1) to see if a more sophisticated weighting can beat the simple inverse_error weighting.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"w1"}

Thought: Test a robust median combination on the full pool to see if it beats the weighted w1 result.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool_full"}

Thought: Test a trimmed‑mean combination on the full pool to see if trimming improves over median.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"trimmed_mean","pool":"pool_full","trim_pct":0.2}

Thought: Test the best single model hypothesis with ONLY_DWT_catboost to see if a single strong model beats the robust combinations.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"best_single","model":"ONLY_DWT_catboost"}

Thought: Test a weighted combination on the reduced pool1 to see if a small, focused pool improves over the best single.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool1","weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: Test a data‑driven baseline adjustment (dba) on the full pool to see if it can beat the best single model.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"dba","pool":"pool_full","dba_max_iter":30}

Thought: Test a weighted combination on the broader pool2 using inverse_error to see if expanding the pool improves over the best single.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool2","weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: Test a weighted combination with inverse_error on the smaller, focused pool3 to see if a tighter set of models improves over the best single.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool3","weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: Test a simple mean over the focused pool1 to see if reducing variance helps compared to weighted.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"mean","pool":"pool1","rationale":"Mean of reduced pool to reduce noise"}

Thought: Test a trimmed‑mean combination on pool2 to see if trimming improves over the weighted pool2 result.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"trimmed_mean","pool":"pool2","trim_pct":0.2}

